- Mermaid is the only diagram provider because it already covers timeline, mindmap,
  flowchart, sequence and ER families; offer those choices in the diagram insertion
  UI before registering another provider. KaTeX math for LitRPG stat blocks isn't a diagram provider: inline math is a
  mark or an inline node, not a fence the page draws instead of showing.

## Native selection and composition

Remaining native-input failures:

1. A selected diagram before empty prose can restart Chromium composition,
   leaving provisional `ni` beside committed `你`. A trace places native focus
   inside the rendered SVG after the first input, before ProseMirror reads the
   DOM. A whole selected table whose last cell ends in a rendered diagram also
   restarts composition, but its input-event trace still shows focus in the typed
   text; whether these share a cause is unproved. To reproduce, place a rendered
   Mermaid diagram before an empty paragraph, or in the last table cell; select
   the diagram or whole table, then compose `ni` → `你`. Expected: exactly `你`
   after the diagram, or in the paragraph after the whole table. Actual: `ni你`.
2. A diagram-only or figure-only document can lose its native range after
   mouseup while ProseMirror keeps a NodeSelection. Chromium then emits no input
   events. Create a document containing only that object, click its body, release
   the mouse, then type. The range can disappear and nothing is inserted. Whether
   this shares the composition-restart cause above is unproved. Fix the missing
   browser input target without per-object event patches.
3. An inline image alone in its paragraph can restart composition even when a
   plain caret is already after it. This reproduces without ProseMirror in static
   contenteditable HTML: an inline-block wrapper containing a block-level image
   box triggers Chromium's restart. An inline-level image box fixes that reduction,
   but the app's hovered chrome introduces another trigger not yet isolated. Fix
   the image/chrome box structure rather than filtering provisional text. Native
   selection projection alone does not fix this case. Insert an inline image beside
   one character, delete that character, click the image and press Right to place
   a caret after it. Compose `ni` → `你`: expected `你`, actual `ni你`. Repeat with
   the pointer over and away from the image to distinguish hover chrome.

Reproduce with real selection plus Chromium `Input.imeSetComposition` updates and
commit. This does not verify Android InputConnection or an operating-system IME.

- Native range preparation has two accepted no-movement limits in Chromium/Linux:
  select a whole table that is last in its document, then Shift+PageDown or
  Ctrl+Shift+Right. The selection narrows to the head cell's text; no text changes.
  CellSelection covers all selected cells, but its native endpoints cover only
  that cell. The [selection representation task](../../.context/TODO.md#cell-selection-restoration)
  tracks this mismatch alongside peer restoration; a shared fix is not yet proved.
  Do not add a key-specific edge guard or a delayed selection rollback.

- A whole selected table at the end of a document can leave provisional `n` when
  composing `n` → `ni` → committed `你` into a newly created trailing paragraph.
  Chromium emits two composition starts and leaves `n你`; starting with `ni`
  instead was exact. A table with an existing following paragraph is exact with
  either sequence. The failure also reproduces with native projection and the
  native key route disabled in the same build. Investigate destination creation
  during composition; its relation to the other restart cases is unproved.
